 we correct?\n# Let's compute: for each sample, what's the bias of base at h0 vs hist_last?\n# And how does that predict future bias?\nprint()\nprint('=== History as error predictor ===')\n# Use the difference between base[h=0] and hist[-1] as a 'recent drift' measure\ndrift0 = base[:, 0, :] - history[:, -1, :]\n\nfor h in [0, 3, 6, 9, 11]:\n    m = mask[:, h, :]\n    resid = base[:, h, :] - targets[:, h, :]\n    corr = np.corrcoef(drift0[m], resid[m])[0, 1]\n    print(f'  h={h}: corr(base_h0 - hist_last, base_h - target) = {corr:.4f}')\n\n# How about using the history trend?\nhist_trend = (history[:, -1, :] - history[:, 0, :]) / 12.0\nfor h in [0, 3, 6, 9, 11]:\n    m = mask[:, h, :]\n    resid = base[:, h, :] - targets[:, h, :]\n    corr = np.corrcoef(hist_trend[m], resid[m])[0, 1]\n    print(f'  h={h}: corr(hist_trend, base_h - target) = {corr:.4f}')\n\n# What about the ratio?\nratio0 = base[:, 0, :] / np.maximum(history[:, -1, :], 1)\nfor h in [0, 3, 6, 9, 11]:\n    m = mask[:, h, :]\n    resid = base[:, h, :] - targets[:, h, :]\n    corr = np.corrcoef(ratio0[m], resid[m])[0, 1]\n    print(f'  h={h}: corr(base_h0/hist_last, base_h - target) = {corr:.4f}')\n\n# How good is hist_last as a predictor for each horizon?\nprint()\nprint('=== hist_last as naive forecast ===')\nfor h in range(12):\n    m = mask[:, h, :]\n    mae = np.abs(history[:, -1, :][m] - targets[:, h, :][m]).mean()\n    print(f'  h={h}: MAE = {mae:.3f}')\n\n# What's the optimal blend of base and hist_last for each horizon?\nprint()\nprint('=== Optimal blend base + hist_last ===')\nfor h in range(12):\n    m = mask[:, h, :]\n    best_w, best_mae = 0, float('inf')\n    for w in np.linspace(0, 0.3, 31):\n        pred = (1-w)*base[:,h,:][m] + w*history[:,-1,:][m]\n        mae = np.abs(pred - targets[:,h,:][m]).mean()\n        if mae < best_mae: best_mae, best_w = mae, w\n    print(f'  h={h}: w_hist={best_w:.2f}, MAE={best_mae:.4f}')\n\\\" 2>&1\n\"","aggregated_output":"=== History vs base forecast relationship ===\nhistory shape: (74, 12, 170)\nhistory last step mean: 229.45\nbase h=0 mean: 231.38\ncorr(hist_last, base_h0) = 0.9939\n\n=== base/history ratio per horizon ===\n  h=0: ratio mean=1.0233, median=1.0062\n  h=1: ratio mean=1.0199, median=1.0021\n  h=2: ratio mean=1.0057, median=0.9900\n  h=3: ratio mean=0.9888, median=0.9752\n  h=4: ratio mean=0.9772, median=0.9635\n  h=5: ratio mean=0.9827, median=0.9664\n  h=6: ratio mean=1.0050, median=0.9791\n  h=7: ratio mean=1.0181, median=0.9857\n  h=8: ratio mean=1.0277, median=0.9874\n  h=9: ratio mean=1.0280, median=0.9844\n  h=10: ratio mean=1.0328, median=0.9819\n  h=11: ratio mean=1.0502, median=0.9851\n\nbase_h0 - hist_last: mean=1.172, median=0.966, mae=10.914\nbase_h0 MAE: 12.697\nhist_last MAE (for h0): 16.070\n\n=== History as error predictor ===\n  h=0: corr(base_h0 - hist_last, base_h - target) = 0.0857\n  h=3: corr(base_h0 - hist_last, base_h - target) = 0.0561\n  h=6: corr(base_h0 - hist_last, base_h - target) = 0.0311\n  h=9: corr(base_h0 - hist_last, base_h - target) = 0.0342\n  h=11: corr(base_h0 - hist_last, base_h - target) = -0.0033\n  h=0: corr(hist_trend, base_h - target) = -0.0899\n  h=3: corr(hist_trend, base_h - target) = -0.0275\n  h=6: corr(hist_trend, base_h - target) = -0.0353\n  h=9: corr(hist_trend, base_h - target) = -0.0043\n  h=11: corr(hist_trend, base_h - target) = 0.0267\n  h=0: corr(base_h0/hist_last, base_h - target) = 0.0362\n  h=3: corr(base_h0/hist_last, base_h - target) = 0.0219\n  h=6: corr(base_h0/hist_last, base_h - target) = 0.0066\n  h=9: corr(base_h0/hist_last, base_h - target) = 0.0069\n  h=11: corr(base_h0/hist_last, base_h - target) = -0.0046\n\n=== hist_last as naive forecast ===\n  h=0: MAE = 16.070\n  h=1: MAE = 18.322\n  h=2: MAE = 18.973\n  h=3: MAE = 20.372\n  h=4: MAE = 23.034\n  h=5: MAE = 24.228\n  h=6: MAE = 25.790\n  h=7: MAE = 27.657\n  h=8: MAE = 29.924\n  h=9: MAE = 31.905\n  h=10: MAE = 34.875\n  h=11: MAE = 38.488\n\n=== Optimal blend base + hist_last ===\n  h=0: w_hist=0.07, MAE=12.6787\n  h=1: w_hist=0.01, MAE=13.4134\n  h=2: w_hist=0.04, MAE=13.5359\n  h=3: w_hist=0.06, MAE=13.6535\n  h=4: w_hist=0.01, MAE=14.0903\n  h=5: w_hist=0.02, MAE=14.6580\n  h=6: w_hist=0.01, MAE=15.3140\n  h=7: w_hist=0.00, MAE=15.5993\n  h=8: w_hist=0.00, MAE=16.2889\n  h=9: w_hist=0.00, MAE=16.6009\n  h=10: w_hist=0.00, MAE=16.7702\n  h=11: w_hist=0.00, MAE=17.2183\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"reasoning","text":"Interesting findings:\n1. \n\nFour key findings have been confirmed: history-based features have low correlation with residuals, hist_last outperforms base across all horizons, blending with hist_last brings tiny early horizon improvements, and the base/history ratio follows a U-shaped diurnal pattern. Per-sample bias correction using hist_last is a viable direction, while the time-of-day pattern is too noisy due to limited samples per bin.\n\nI will explore several error correction approaches, including regularized time-of-day bias adjustment, log-domain per-node multiplicative corrections, and cross-validation-tuned shrinkage parameters for existing components. I also plan to investigate the anchor effect and test whether the anchor is a historical average model."}}
