{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_75","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"cd /workspace/solution && python3 -c \\\"\nimport numpy as np\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import Ridge\n\ntrain_feats = np.load('/workspace/public_assets/train_features.npz')\ntrain_targets = np.load('/workspace/public_assets/train_targets.npz')\n\nbase = train_feats['base'].astype(np.float64)\ntargets = train_targets['target'].astype(np.float64)\nanchor = train_feats['anchor'].astype(np.float64)\nhistory = train_feats['history'].astype(np.float64)\nclock = train_feats['clock'].astype(np.float64)\n\nn_samples, n_horizons, n_nodes = base.shape\nmask = np.isfinite(targets) & (targets > 0)\n\ndef cv_evaluate(predict_fn, n_folds=5, seed=42):\n    rng = np.random.RandomState(seed)\n    indices = np.arange(n_samples)\n    rng.shuffle(indices)\n    fold_size = n_samples // n_folds\n    maes = []\n    for fold in range(n_folds):\n        val_start = fold * fold_size\n        val_end = val_start + fold_size if fold < n_folds-1 else n_samples\n        val_idx = indices[val_start:val_end]\n        train_idx = np.setdiff1d(indices, val_idx)\n        pred = predict_fn(train_idx, val_idx)\n        m = mask[val_idx]\n        mae = np.abs(pred[m] - targets[val_idx][m]).mean()\n        maes.append(mae)\n    return np.mean(maes), np.std(maes)\n\n# Full v23 as reference\ndef v23_pred(train_idx, val_idx):\n    b_tr, t_tr = base[train_idx], targets[train_idx]\n    a_tr, h_tr = anchor[train_idx], history[train_idx]\n    c_tr = clock[train_idx]\n    m_tr = mask[train_idx]\n    b_va, a_va = base[val_idx], anchor[val_idx]\n    h_va, c_va = history[val_idx], clock[val_idx]\n    nh, nn = n_horizons, n_nodes\n    ns_tr = len(train_idx)\n    ns_va = len(val_idx)\n    \n    anchor_h = np.zeros(nh)\n    for h in range(nh):\n        m = m_tr[:, h, :]\n        best_mae, best_w = float('inf'), 0\n        for w in np.linspace(0, 0.30, 31):\n            pred = (1-w)*b_tr[:,h,:][m] + w*a_tr[:,h,:][m]\n            mae = np.abs(pred - t_tr[:,h,:][m]).mean()\n            if mae < best_mae: best_mae, best_w = mae, w\n        anchor_h[h] = best_w\n    \n    pna_shrink = 0.2\n    anchor_nh = np.zeros((nh, nn))\n    for h in range(nh):\n        for n in range(nn):\n            m = m_tr[:, h, n]\n            if m.sum() > 15:\n                best_mae, best_w = float('inf'), anchor_h[h]\n                for w in np.linspace(0, 0.40, 21):\n                    pred = (1-w)*b_tr[:,h,n][m] + w*a_tr[:,h,n][m]\n                    mae = np.abs(pred - t_tr[:,h,n][m]).mean()\n                    if mae < best_mae: best_mae, best_w = mae, w\n                anchor_nh[h,n] = best_w\n            else:\n                anchor_nh[h,n] = anchor_h[h]\n    anchor_nh = pna_shrink * anchor_nh + (1-pna_shrink) * anchor_h[:, np.newaxis]\n    \n    blended_tr = (1-anchor_nh[np.newaxis,:,:])*b_tr + anchor_nh[np.newaxis,:,:]*a_tr\n    blended_va = (1-anchor_nh[np.newaxis,:,:])*b_va + anchor_nh[np.newaxis,:,:]*a_va\n    \n    h_bias = np.zeros(nh)\n    for h in range(nh):\n        m = m_tr[:, h, :]\n        h_bias[h] = np.median(blended_tr[:,h,:][m] - t_tr[:,h,:][m])\n    corrected_tr = blended_tr - h_bias[np.newaxis,:,np.newaxis]\n    corrected_va = blended_va - h_bias[np.newaxis,:,np.newaxis]\n    \n    node_shrink = 0.4\n    node_bias = np.zeros(nn)\n    res_tr = corrected_tr - t_tr\n    for n in range(nn):\n        m = m_tr[:, :, n]\n        if m.sum() > 5:\n            node_bias[n] = np.median(res_tr[:,:,n][m])\n    node_bias = node_shrink * node_bias\n    corrected_tr = corrected_tr - node_bias[np.newaxis, np.newaxis, :]\n    corrected_va = corrected_va - node_bias[np.newaxis, np.newaxis, :]\n    \n    pnh_shrink = 0.15\n    bias_nh = np.zeros((nh, nn))\n    res_tr = corrected_tr - t_tr\n    for h in range(nh):\n        for n in range(nn):\n            m = m_tr[:, h, n]\n            if m.sum() > 0:\n                bias_nh[h,n] = pnh_shrink * np.median(res_tr[:,h,n][m])\n    corrected_tr = corrected_tr - bias_nh[np.newaxis,:,:]\n    corrected_va = corrected_va - bias_nh[np.newaxis,:,:]\n    \n    mult_shrink = 0.5\n    mult_factor = np.ones(nn)\n    for n in range(nn):\n        m = m_tr[:, :, n]\n        p = corrected_tr[:,:,n][m]\n        tgt = t_tr[:,:,n][m]\n        if m.sum() > 20 and np.min(p) > 1:\n            mult_factor[n] = np.median(tgt / p)\n    mult_factor = 1.0 + mult_shrink * (mult_factor - 1.0)\n    corrected_tr = corrected_tr * mult_factor[np.newaxis, np.newaxis, :]\n    corrected_va = corrected_va * mult_factor[np.newaxis, np.newaxis, :]\n    res_tr = corrected_tr - t_tr\n    \n    # Ridge (v23 params)\n    ridge_alpha = 1000.0\n    ridge_shrink = 0.3\n    hist_last_tr = h_tr[:, -1, :]\n    hist_avg_tr = h_tr.mean(axis=1)\n    hist_trend_tr = (h_tr[:, -1, :] - h_tr[:, 0, :]) / 12.0\n    hist_last_va = h_va[:, -1, :]\n    hist_avg_va = h_va.mean(axis=1)\n    hist_trend_va = (h_va[:, -1, :] - h_va[:, 0, :]) / 12.0\n    \n    for h in range(nh):\n        m = m_tr[:, h, :]\n        y = res_tr[:, h, :][m].flatten()\n        if len(y) < 100: continue\n        node_idx_flat = np.tile(np.arange(nn), (ns_tr, 1)).reshape(-1, 1)\n        X = np.hstack([\n            b_tr[:, h, :].reshape(-1, 1),\n            a_tr[:, h, :].reshape(-1, 1),\n            hist_last_tr.reshape(-1, 1),\n            hist_avg_tr.reshape(-1, 1),\n            hist_trend_tr.reshape(-1, 1),\n            np.sin(2 * np.pi * np.repeat(c_tr[:, h, 0], nn)).reshape(-1, 1),\n            np.cos(2 * np.pi * np.repeat(c_tr[:, h, 0], nn)).reshape(-1, 1),\n            np.sin(2 * np.pi * node_idx_flat / nn),\n            np.cos(2 * np.pi * node_idx_flat / nn),\n        ])\n        X_valid = X[m.flatten()]\n        mu = X_valid.mean(axis=0)\n        sd = X_valid.std(axis=0)\n        sd[sd < 1e-6] = 1.0\n        Xs = (X_valid - mu) / sd\n        model = Ridge(alpha=ridge_alpha, fit_intercept=True)\n        model.fit(Xs, y)\n        \n        node_idx_flat_v = np.tile(np.arange(nn), (ns_va, 1)).reshape(-1, 1)\n        Xv = np.hstack([\n            b_va[:, h, :].reshape(-1, 1),\n            a_va[:, h, :].reshape(-1, 1),\n            hist_last_va.reshape(-1, 1),\n            hist_avg_va.reshape(-1, 1),\n            hist_trend_va.reshape(-1, 1),\n            np.sin(2 * np.pi * np.repeat(c_va[:, h, 0], nn)).reshape(-1, 1),\n            np.cos(2 * np.pi * np.repeat(c_va[:, h, 0], nn)).reshape(-1, 1),\n            np.sin(2 * np.pi * node_idx_flat_v / nn),\n            np.cos(2 * np.pi * node_idx_flat_v / nn),\n        ])\n        Xvs = (Xv - mu) / sd\n        correction = ridge_shrink * (Xvs @ model.coef_ + model.intercept_)\n        corrected_va[:, h, :] = corrected_va[:, h, :] - correction.reshape(ns_va, nn)\n    \n    return np.maximum(corrected_va, 0.0)\n\n# Baseline v23\nmaes = []\nfor seed in [42, 123, 777]:\n    mae, _ = cv_evaluate(v23_pred, seed=seed)\n    maes.append(mae)\nprint(f'v23 baseline: avg={np.mean(maes):.4f} ({[f\\\\\\\"{m:.4f}\\\\\\\" for m in maes]})')\n\n# ============================================================\n# Test: Conservative per-sample bias correction BEFORE ridge\n# Simple model: per-horizon slope only (no intercept), \n#   sample_resid = slope * mean(base - anchor)\n# Strong shrinkage\n# ============================================================\ndef v23_plus_samplebias(sample_shrink=0.2, use_intercept=False):\n    def predict_fn(train_idx, val_idx):\n        b_tr, t_tr = base[train_idx], targets[train_idx]\n        a_tr, h_tr = anchor[train_idx], history[train_idx]\n        c_tr = clock[train_idx]\n        m_tr = mask[train_idx]\n        b_va, a_va = base[val_idx], anchor[val_idx]\n        h_va, c_va = history[val_idx], clock[val_idx]\n        nh, nn = n_horizons, n_nodes\n        ns_tr = len(train_idx)\n        ns_va = len(val_idx)\n        \n        anchor_h = np.zeros(nh)\n        for h in range(nh):\n            m = m_tr[:, h, :]\n            best_mae, best_w = float('inf'), 0\n            for w in np.linspace(0, 0.30, 31):\n                pred = (1-w)*b_tr[:,h,:][m] + w*a_tr[:,h,:][m]\n                mae = np.abs(pred - t_tr[:,h,:][m]).mean()\n                if mae < best_mae: best_mae, best_w = mae, w\n            anchor_h[h] = best_w\n        \n        pna_shrink = 0.2\n        anchor_nh = np.zeros((nh, nn))\n        for h in range(nh):\n            for n in range(nn):\n                m = m_tr[:, h, n]\n                if m.sum() > 15:\n                    best_mae, best_w = float('inf'), anchor_h[h]\n                    for w in np.linspace(0, 0.40, 21):\n                        pred = (1-w)*b_tr[:,h,n][m] + w*a_tr[:,h,n][m]\n                        mae = np.abs(pred - t_tr[:,h,n][m]).mean()\n                        if mae < best_mae: best_mae, best_w = mae, w\n                    anchor_nh[h,n] = best_w\n                else:\n                    anchor_nh[h,n] = anchor_h[h]\n        anchor_nh = pna_shrink * anchor_nh + (1-pna_shrink) * anchor_h[:, np.newaxis]\n        \n        blended_tr = (1-anchor_nh[np.newaxis,:,:])*b_tr + anchor_nh[np.newaxis,:,:]*a_tr\n        blended_va = (1-anchor_nh[np.newaxis,:,:])*b_va + anchor_nh[np.newaxis,:,:]*a_va\n        \n        h_bias = np.zeros(nh)\n        for h in range(nh):\n            m = m_tr[:, h, :]\n            h_bias[h] = np.median(blended_tr[:,h,:][m] - t_tr[:,h,:][m])\n        corrected_tr = blended_tr - h_bias[np.newaxis,:,np.newaxis]\n        corrected_va = blended_va - h_bias[np.newaxis,:,np.newaxis]\n        \n        node_shrink = 0.4\n        node_bias = np.zeros(nn)\n        res_tr = corrected_tr - t_tr\n        for n in range(nn):\n            m = m_tr[:, :, n]\n            if m.sum() > 5:\n                node_bias[n] = np.median(res_tr[:,:,n][m])\n        node_bias = node_shrink * node_bias\n        corrected_tr = corrected_tr - node_bias[np.newaxis, np.newaxis, :]\n        corrected_va = corrected_va - node_bias[np.newaxis, np.newaxis, :]\n        \n        pnh_shrink = 0.15\n        bias_nh = np.zeros((nh, nn))\n        res_tr = corrected_tr - t_tr\n        for h in range(nh):\n            for n in range(nn):\n                m = m_tr[:, h, n]\n                if m.sum() > 0:\n                    bias_nh[h,n] = pnh_shrink * np.median(res_tr[:,h,n][m])\n        corrected_tr = corrected_tr - bias_nh[np.newaxis,:,:]\n        corrected_va = corrected_va - bias_nh[np.newaxis,:,:]\n        \n        mult_shrink = 0.5\n        mult_factor = np.ones(nn)\n        for n in range(nn):\n            m = m_tr[:, :, n]\n            p = corrected_tr[:,:,n][m]\n            tgt = t_tr[:,:,n][m]\n            if m.sum() > 20 and np.min(p) > 1:\n                mult_factor[n] = np.median(tgt / p)\n        mult_factor = 1.0 + mult_shrink * (mult_factor - 1.0)\n        corrected_tr = corrected_tr * mult_factor[np.newaxis, np.newaxis, :]\n        corrected_va = corrected_va * mult_factor[np.newaxis, np.newaxis, :]\n        res_tr = corrected_tr - t_tr\n        \n        # Per-sample bias correction (simple slope-only)\n        sample_ba_tr = np.zeros((ns_tr, nh))\n        sample_resid_tr = np.zeros((ns_tr, nh))\n        for h in range(nh):\n            for i in range(ns_tr):\n                mi = m_tr[i, h, :]\n                if mi.sum() > 0:\n                    sample_ba_tr[i, h] = (b_tr[i, h, :][mi] - a_tr[i, h, :][mi]).mean()\n                    sample_resid_tr[i, h] = res_tr[i, h, :][mi].mean()\n        \n        sample_ba_va = np.zeros((ns_va, nh))\n        for h in range(nh):\n            sample_ba_va[:, h] = (b_va[:, h, :] - a_va[:, h, :]).mean(axis=1)\n        \n        sample_slope = np.zeros(nh)\n        sample_intercept = np.zeros(nh)\n        for h in range(nh):\n            valid = np.isfinite(sample_resid_tr[:, h]) & np.isfinite(sample_ba_tr[:, h])\n            if valid.sum() < 10: continue\n            x = sample_ba_tr[valid, h]\n            y = sample_resid_tr[valid, h]\n            if use_intercept:\n                X = np.column_stack([np.ones(len(x)), x])\n                alpha_reg = 10.0\n                coef = np.linalg.lstsq(X.T @ X + alpha_reg * np.eye(2), X.T @ y, rcond=None)[0]\n                sample_intercept[h] = coef[0]\n                sample_slope[h] = coef[1]\n            else:\n                # slope only, no intercept (since per-horizon bias already handles the mean)\n                # ridge regression: min ||y - x*b||\"'^2 + alpha*b''^2\n                alpha_reg = 10.0\n                sample_slope[h] = np.dot(x, y) / (np.dot(x, x) + alpha_reg)\n        \n        # Apply per-sample correction\n        for h in range(nh):\n            pred_bias = sample_intercept[h] + sample_slope[h] * sample_ba_va[:, h]\n            corrected_va[:, h, :] = corrected_va[:, h, :] - sample_shrink * pred_bias[:, np.newaxis]\n            # Also update training residuals for ridge\n            pred_bias_tr = sample_intercept[h] + sample_slope[h] * sample_ba_tr[:, h]\n            corrected_tr[:, h, :] = corrected_tr[:, h, :] - sample_shrink * pred_bias_tr[:, np.newaxis]\n        \n        res_tr = corrected_tr - t_tr\n        \n        # Ridge (v23 params)\n        ridge_alpha = 1000.0\n        ridge_shrink = 0.3\n        hist_last_tr = h_tr[:, -1, :]\n        hist_avg_tr = h_tr.mean(axis=1)\n        hist_trend_tr = (h_tr[:, -1, :] - h_tr[:, 0, :]) / 12.0\n        hist_last_va = h_va[:, -1, :]\n        hist_avg_va = h_va.mean(axis=1)\n        hist_trend_va = (h_va[:, -1, :] - h_va[:, 0, :]) / 12.0\n        \n        for h in range(nh):\n            m = m_tr[:, h, :]\n            y = res_tr[:, h, :][m].flatten()\n            if len(y) < 100: continue\n            node_idx_flat = np.tile(np.arange(nn), (ns_tr, 1)).reshape(-1, 1)\n            X = np.hstack([\n                b_tr[:, h, :].reshape(-1, 1),\n                a_tr[:, h, :].reshape(-1, 1),\n                hist_last_tr.reshape(-1, 1),\n                hist_avg_tr.reshape(-1, 1),\n                hist_trend_tr.reshape(-1, 1),\n                np.sin(2 * np.pi * np.repeat(c_tr[:, h, 0], nn)).reshape(-1, 1),\n                np.cos(2 * np.pi * np.repeat(c_tr[:, h, 0], nn)).reshape(-1, 1),\n                np.sin(2 * np.pi * node_idx_flat / nn),\n                np.cos(2 * np.pi * node_idx_flat / nn),\n            ])\n            X_valid = X[m.flatten()]\n            mu = X_valid.mean(axis=0)\n            sd = X_valid.std(axis=0)\n            sd[sd < 1e-6] = 1.0\n            Xs = (X_valid - mu) / sd\n            model = Ridge(alpha=ridge_alpha, fit_intercept=True)\n            model.fit(Xs, y)\n            \n            node_idx_flat_v = np.tile(np.arange(nn), (ns_va, 1)).reshape(-1, 1)\n            Xv = np.hstack([\n                b_va[:, h, :].reshape(-1, 1),\n                a_va[:, h, :].reshape(-1, 1),\n                hist_last_va.reshape(-1, 1),\n                hist_avg_va.reshape(-1, 1),\n                hist_trend_va.reshape(-1, 1),\n                np.sin(2 * np.pi * np.repeat(c_va[:, h, 0], nn)).reshape(-1, 1),\n                np.cos(2 * np.pi * np.repeat(c_va[:, h, 0], nn)).reshape(-1, 1),\n                np.sin(2 * np.pi * node_idx_flat_v / nn),\n                np.cos(2 * np.pi * node_idx_flat_v / nn),\n            ])\n            Xvs = (Xv - mu) / sd\n            correction = ridge_shrink * (Xvs @ model.coef_ + model.intercept_)\n            corrected_va[:, h, :] = corrected_va[:, h, :] - correction.reshape(ns_va, nn)\n        \n        return np.maximum(corrected_va, 0.0)\n    return predict_fn\n\nprint()\nprint('\"'=== v23 + per-sample bias correction ===')\nfor shrink in [0.1, 0.15, 0.2, 0.3, 0.4]:\n    for intercept in [False, True]:\n        maes = []\n        for seed in [42, 123, 777]:\n            mae, _ = cv_evaluate(v23_plus_samplebias(shrink, intercept), seed=seed)\n            maes.append(mae)\n        print(f'  shrink={shrink:.2f}, intercept={intercept}: avg={np.mean(maes):.4f} ({[f\\\\\\\"{m:.4f}\\\\\\\" for m in maes]})')\n\\\" 2>&1\n\"","aggregated_output":"v23 baseline: avg=14.4238 (['14.4880', '14.3616', '14.4217'])\n\n=== v23 + per-sample bias correction ===\n  shrink=0.10, intercept=False: avg=14.4182 (['14.4823', '14.3550', '14.4172'])\n  shrink=0.10, intercept=True: avg=14.4178 (['14.4819', '14.3548', '14.4166'])\n  shrink=0.15, intercept=False: avg=14.4157 (['14.4798', '14.3520', '14.4153'])\n  shrink=0.15, intercept=True: avg=14.4152 (['14.4793', '14.3518', '14.4144'])\n  shrink=0.20, intercept=False: avg=14.4134 (['14.4775', '14.3492', '14.4135'])\n  shrink=0.20, intercept=True: avg=14.4128 (['14.4770', '14.3490', '14.4125'])\n  shrink=0.30, intercept=False: avg=14.4094 (['14.4736', '14.3440', '14.4107'])\n  shrink=0.30, intercept=True: avg=14.4089 (['14.4731', '14.3440', '14.4095'])\n  shrink=0.40, intercept=False: avg=14.4062 (['14.4705', '14.3394', '14.4088'])\n  shrink=0.40, intercept=True: avg=14.4059 (['14.4704', '14.3398', '14.4075'])\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_77","type":"reasoning","text":"The per-sample bias correction shows small improvements in CV:\n- v23 baseline: avg=14.4238\n- Best: shrink=0.40, The intercept=True setting brings a ~0.018 MAE CV improvement, which is small, consistent across seeds and far less invasive than the v24 change. I’ll test a shrinkage value of 0.2 on the public scorer, but note the dev set’s noise means the improvement may not show up, and there is a risk of performance loss.\n\nI’ve put forward four alternative optimization approaches, including graph-regularized per-node bias correction, ensemble with simpler methods, median-based loss adjustment and leave-one-sample-out CV for hyperparameter tuning. I’ve decided to adopt the first approach, as residuals show spatial correlation and the graph has useful spatial structure.\n\nI’ve finalized the implementation details of the graph-regularized per-node bias correction, and will test the shrink=0.2 per-sample bias correction first as a conservative approach. I’ll also try ensemble averaging and graph-smoothed anchor blending later, and will first analyze the root cause of v24’s failure.\n\nAnalysis shows v24's performance gap between CV and dev widened by 0.09, caused by overfitting from its extra parameters. The simpler per-sample bias correction is more secure, so I’ll give it a try."}}
